dsv41 patch 0062 (21.10.2026): the DSpark verify step's sampling phase on the live rows only (variant 2b of an exact
verify width per round). Off: expected 0.03-0.25 % per round, below what our A/B resolves; built (image v13), not
measured, not in v19. Base: the v12 file vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py; new file
vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/exact_verify.py.
Why: with the per-round depth policy a verify window keeps its scheduled shape (k + 1 rows per request); rows past a
request's depth ("dead rows") skip only the routed experts and are rejected as invalid drafts, so at 1 stream a dead
row still costs ~0.2-0.25 ms (dense layers, attention). TensorFold sizes its rounds to the drafts it verifies. On 21.10.
a re-measured round-cost table made the depth policy choose shallower rounds without saving time (tok/s -0.20 %; prose
at T=0: ms per round -2.7 %, tokens per round -5.0 %). A forward of exact width does not fit this stack: the host would
need the depth before it launches the target graph, but the DeepSeek-V4.1 attention metadata (indexer next_n,
short-context twins, SWA and compressor builders) is planned on the host from the CPU query lengths; the V4.1 indexer
accepts a device/host query-length mismatch only on sm90/sm100, not on GB10; re-planning after a sync would, by our
estimate, cost more host time than the dead rows (in a profiled round of 19.10. the host spent 5.2 ms from the block
tables to the last SWA metadata and 0.9-6.1 ms in the graph launch call); and another row count picks other kernels, so
T=0 texts would change. The sampling phase runs eagerly after the target graph has been launched, and the depth was
chosen before that graph in stream order: waiting for it on the host costs the GPU nothing.
How (exact_verify.py, hooks in model_runner.py): prepare_inputs copies the depth policy's dead-row mask (one bool per
logits row) to pinned host memory behind an event; sample() waits for it, builds the live layout (the stock path unless
every request's dead rows are its tail), computes the logits of the live rows (head and all-gather on the live rows
when the window runs the exl3_mrow head, else the head on the window and only the all-gather and the sampler on the
live rows), runs the stock rejection sampler on them and recomputes num_rejected against the full window, so the
drafter, the depth-policy statistics and the scheduler see what they see without the switch. Structured outputs,
logprobs, sampling masks, watermarking, block / synthetic verification, batch-sharded sampling and PP / PCP keep the
stock path. Same tokens by construction: greedy, the token after the last live row is that row's argmax in both paths
(lowest index on ties); sampled, a resample of that row's target distribution keyed by the same (seed, position). No
new CUDA graphs, no device memory. VLLM_DSV41_EXACT_VERIFY=count only counts: stock sampling and a "DSV41_EV" log line
every VLLM_DSV41_EV_LOG steps with window / live / dead verify rows by request count.
Tested offline (CPU): a Python port of the V2 rejection kernels, 3000 random cases with forced logit ties, greedy and
sampled: tokens, num_sampled and num_rejected identical; two deliberate mutations (tie order, live-relative
num_rejected) are caught; a module test against the stock sample() flow with stand-ins for head, all-gather and sampler.
Not measured on GB10 (expected ~0.01-0.04 ms per dead row: head rows, a 129 KB all-gather per row, sampler passes).
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_EXACT_VERIFY=1 (exact sampling phase) | count (statistics only) | 0 (default, off: the runner never
creates the helper); VLLM_DSV41_EV_LOG=N (default VLLM_DSPARK_DEPTH_LOG, else 256 with count). Only with the depth
policy, which decides the live rows.

